   Energy, Environment and Sustainability (TMREES), Athens, GREECE, SEP
   19-21, 2018},
Abstract = {In recent years, the expansion of Harbin's main urban area, the capital
   city of a northeast province in china, has resulted in the increase of
   impervious surface, the decrease of green space and the significant
   change of urban thermal environment. In order to further reveal the
   comprehensive effects of underlying surface especially green space and
   impervious surface on urban thermal environment in the severe cold
   region, this paper adopts remote sensing technology to extract and
   analyze the Landsat spectral imaging data of Harbin's main urban area in
   summers and winters from 2004 to 2015, and thus puts forward the
   regulations of effects of different underlying surface types on land
   surface temperature (EST). It is found that a large amount of permeable
   underlying surface like green space in Harbin has been continuously
   transformed into impervious surface, which has led to a continuous rise
   of urban land surface temperature in recent years. Urban green space
   plays a certain role in improving urban thermal environment in both
   summers and winters. We can fmd especial rules on the distribution of
   the urban loops and the cooling ranges in summers. As for winters, under
   the influence of the main heat source and the cooling mode, there is no
   remarkable regularity. (C) 2019 The Authors. Published by Elsevier Ltd.},
