   Korean Soc Indoor Environm; Soc Indoor Environm},
Abstract = {Human perception of IAQ ``problems{''} has created significant interest.
   Psychological influences on perception of IAQ are well known. Human
   sensitivity to IAQ contaminates has resulted in cutaneous and
   respiratory track ailments. Cacosmics reporting odour from low
   concentration of chemicals exacerbate SBS concerns. In an IAQ study of a
   high-rise building in Hong Kong, physical IAQ parameters temperature,
   relative humidity, carbon dioxide] are sampled and results are plotted.
   Chemical samples {[}carbon dioxide, nitrogen dioxide and formaldehyde]
   are obtained and results indicate acceptable IAQ based on local and
   international guidelines. However, common complaints of poor IAQ because
   of ``stuffy air{''}, and ``odour{''} from un-identified sources have
   been recorded ever since initial occupancy. From walkthrouh inspection,
   over 72 hours of data logging, and study of pollution pathway, source of
   odour was traced to poorly designed AHU drain-traps. Alteration work was
   carried out, and a follow-up survey was performed. Results are compared
   and reported.},
