   Regeneration, Chung Ang Univ, Dept Urban Design \& Studies, Seoul, SOUTH
   KOREA, AUG 25-27, 2014},
Organization = {Assoc Malaysian Environm Behav Researchers},
Abstract = {The property industry acts as vital sector whereby the service
   environment directly correlates the customers' behavioral intention in
   purchasing a property. However, to date, a study regarding service
   environment and its impact still not fully addressed in the property
   industry. Thus, the purpose of this study is to investigate the
   relationship between service environment and customers' behavioral
   intention moderated by income in Malaysian property industry. A total of
   357 respondents participated in this study by using a convenience
   sampling. The result shown that lower middle income was significantly
   moderated the relationship between service environment and customers'
   behavioral intention. (C) 2015 The Authors. Published by Elsevier Ltd.},
