   Management},
Abstract = {Since reform and opening up, the economic development of Yangtze River
   Delta has always been at the forefront of China. In this article, we
   selected 22 indicators, which came from different respects including
   economy, population, education, industry, government and environment, to
   calculate the urban comprehensive development index (CDI) of 25 cities
   in Yangtze River Delta by employing the entropy weighting method. In
   combination with spatial autocorrelation analysis, we found that: The
   cities in Northern Zhejiang developed more quickly than Southern
   Jiangsu, and the development of urban agglomeration in Yangtze River
   Delta showed significant agglomeration characteristics in spatial
   distribution. According to the results of entropy weighting, the
   government, FDI, science and education, environment, and factors
   mobility were the important factors to influence the integration process
   of Yangtze River Delta. And the Integration of urban agglomeration was
   based on the well-developed industrialization and urbanization of area,
   and its impetus came mainly from the aggregation and dispersion effect
   of central cities, industrial development and regional division of
   labor, the government support, scientific and technological advancement
   as well as environmental improvement. Finally, we stimulated the
   evolution of spatial structure of urban agglomeration in Yangtze River
   Delta through C-means fuzzy clustering model and GIS technology.},
