   \& Remote Sensing Soc},
Abstract = {The environmental health of coastal metropolis has not only influenced
   by rapid urbanization but always undergone the ecological pressures and
   dual risks from both the terrestrial and aquatic systems. Taking
   Guangzhou, Hangzhou, and Shanghai, three metropolises of China as
   examples, this study aims to disclose and compare the spatiotemporal
   characteristics and variations of the thermal environments in different
   coastal metropolises under the land cover/use scenario. It is expected
   that the finding from this study would provide valuable clues for future
   sustainability in the coastal metropolis.},
