   22-24, 1996},
Organization = {Neurootol Equilibriometr Soc},
Abstract = {The authors are presenting the statistical results of a study concerning
   the affection of the vestibular function in patients with sensorial
   hearing loss. The study was performed between 1.01.1994-31.12.1995, in
   the Department of Audiology, University ENT Clinic `'Coltea'',
   Bucharest.
   216 cases of sensorial hearing loss of different etiologies, e.g.
   (oto)toxic hearing loss, noise induced hearing loss, presbyacousia,
   acoustic neurinoma, were included in the study. Cases of otosclerosis,
   chronic suppurative otomastoiditis, Meniere disease as well as
   congenital deafness were excluded.
   The conclusion of the study is that for the complete diagnosis of some
   types of hearing loss, the vestibular investigation is of great
   importance.},
