Note = {3rd International Conference on Energy and Development - Environment -
   Biomedicine, Vouliagmeni, GREECE, DEC 29-30, 2009},
Organization = {N Atlantic Univ Union},
Abstract = {Among the many problems that threaten human-environment report, for
   human life, wastes and their management arc, without doubt, major
   problems.
   Waste represents those substances or objects which the holder discards
   or intends or is required to be discarded. In general, waste is the last
   stage of the life cycle of a product (the time between the date of
   manufacture of the product and the date when it becomes waste).
   The waste management problem manifests itself more strongly, due to
   increased quantity and variety of them and their negative impact, more
   pronounced, exerted on the environment. Storing them on the ground
   without satisfying the minimum requirements, discharge them on water
   courses and their uncontrolled burning is a major downside for both the
   environment and human health.
   In this respect, European law, as expressed by national regulatory acts,
   required a new approach to the issue submitted to, from the need to
   conserve natural resources to the reduce management costs and find
   efficient solutions in the reduction of negative environmental impacts.
   In the year 2008, municipal solid waste results in urban areas of the
   county Dambovita were collected were mixed and stored in the six
   municipal landfills (Aninoasa - Targoviste, Pucioasa, Fieni, Moreni,
   Gaesti, Titu), in a simple manner, without any measure of control of
   pollution of groundwater and surface water, in terms of biological,
   bacteriological, physical and chemical.},
