   Delft, NETHERLANDS, SEP 28-30, 2011},
Organization = {Urban Data Management Soc; Int Soc Photogrammetry \& Remote Sensing; Int
   Soc Photogrammetry \& Remote Sensing Commiss IV Geodatabases \& Digital
   Mapping; Working Grp IV 8 3D Spatial Data Integrat Disaster Management
   \& Environm Monitoring; Delft Univ Technol},
Abstract = {This paper presents the use of 3D GIS to represent, analyse and explore
   the most common urban rules described in French local urban planning
   schemes. As these rules are only expressed in free formed texts, it is
   difficult to assess their impact on the evolution of the urban
   environment. A schema is proposed in order to allow the capture and
   management of urban rules. These rules are applied to a structured
   geographic environment in order to automatically determine and represent
   their influence by 3D volumes. Three different applications of the
   proposed model are explored in this article: (1) to asses or emulate the
   influence of urban rules in terms of potential constructions (by visual
   analysis), (2) to determine their influence on the Floor Area Ratio (by
   spatial analysis), (3) to evaluate pre-project building shapes.},
