Note = {4th International Conference on Modern Research in Psychology - Trends
   and Prospects, Sibiu, ROMANIA, JUN 03-05, 2011},
Abstract = {The aim of this study is to identify the correlations between the
   emotion regulation strategies, difficulties in emotion regulation and
   well being in young people. The aspects of emotions regulation
   difficulties that were investigated in this study are: Control of
   impulses difficulties (IMPULSE), Nonacceptance of Emotional Responses
   (NONACCEPTANCE), Difficulties Engaging in Goal Directed (GOALS), Lack of
   Emotional Awareness (AWARENESS), Limited Access to Emotion Regulation
   Strategies (STRAIEGIES), Lack of Emotional Clarity (CLARITY). Subjective
   life satisfaction values were used to asses the well being of the
   person. The considered emotion regulation strategies are expressive
   suppression and cognitive reappraisal that the literature demonstrated
   the important impact of the use of these two mechanisms for physical and
   mental health. The research was developed on a sample of 160 young
   people with ages between 15 23 years. The results demonstrated for the
   reappraisal group a decreasing of the control of impulses difficulties,
   difficulties in engaging goal directed and limited access to emotion
   regulation strategies and increasing of life satisfaction.},
