   Educ Sci, Bucharest, ROMANIA, OCT 24-26, 2014},
Organization = {Romanian Soc Appl Expt Psychol},
Abstract = {The purpose of the study was to explore the positive and negative
   emotions of young Romanian couples in terms of what do they usually
   express, how they consider is adequate to express them and what are the
   reasons for which they consider expressing them. 98 participants
   (57women and 45 men; age M=26.4, minimum 20, maximum 45 years old)
   responded, more than 350 words/expression were analyzed for each of the
   considered topics. Results show that the Romanian specific cultural
   heritance prevails - young Romania couples face difficulties in
   recognizing and expressing their emotions, even though they are aware of
   the related benefits. Gender differences still need to be furthered
   explored, but confirm the enforced alexithymia mainly upon men. (C) 2015
   The Authors. Published by Elsevier Ltd.},
