Note = {2nd Advanced Research on Business, Management and Humanities (ARBUHUM),
   Phuket, THAILAND, OCT 10-12, 2017},
Organization = {Malaysia Tech Scientist Assoc},
Abstract = {Customer perceptions are the customer's beliefs, feelings, and behaviour
   regarding banking services. These perceptions can decide the success or
   failure of the bank. This study examines the factors affecting customer
   perceptions in the commercial banking sector of Cambodia. Furthermore,
   this study determines the level of customer perceptions of the
   commercial banks of Cambodia. Primary data was collected from 450
   customers, however, only 402 responses were usable. All the respondents
   were customers of the nine commercial banks in Phnom Penh, Cambodia. The
   results of the Structural Equation Model indicate that brand, personal
   experience and technology (BET) are factors affecting customer
   perception while culture is not significant to customer perception of
   the commercial banking sector of Cambodia. Furthermore, the level of the
   customer perception of the foreign banks is higher than local banks and
   subsidiary banks.},
