Organization = {Int Soc Ecol Modelling},
Abstract = {Industrial factories in urban development zones (UDZs) are a main source
   of both accident risk and aggregate risk. Aggregate risk is an important
   consideration in UDZs because of the potential for harm and serious
   disadvantages. The destruction of ecosystems and environmental disasters
   can occur when the pollutant is hidden and allowed to aggregate to high
   levels. The present paper reviews methods of aggregate risk assessment
   and proposes a program of aggregate risk assessment for UDZs. (C) 2011
   Published by Elsevier B. V. Selection and/or peer-review under
