   Govt Goteborg; Provincial Govt Bohus Ian},
Abstract = {To investigate the spatial and temporal variability of acid deposition
   in the urban environment a small-scale intensive network of bulk
   collectors has been deployed around Greater Manchester, UK. This network
   has been in operation since 1986. The concentrations and deposition
   rates of non-marine (nm) sulphate, nitrate, ammonium, calcium and
   hydrogen are reported for 1994. Acidity was generally lower in the city
   centre of Manchester where calcium concentrations were highest. Calcium
   compounds in the urban atmosphere effectively buffer the precipitation
   acidity.},
