Abstract = {Emotion changes human speech articulation, phonation and respiration in
   such a way that it can be empirically measured. However, no researchers
   can claim superiority on the accuracy since there are many approaches
   implemented but it is very much dependant on the data used as well as
   influencing factors such as cultural effects. In this paper, homogeneous
   intra-cultural speech emotion identification study are conducted using
