   Studies},
Abstract = {The report aims to improve environmental management by integrating and
   making more accessible to managers the information on environmental
   perceptions of the landscape in Kastoria Western Macedonia. First a
   literature review of published surveys of community perceptions of
   landscape values country are reported, and a range of survey methods is
   evaluated for the case. Good-practice benchmarks are identified for each
   method, and criteria for evaluation of this research are analysed. Then
   a methodology is developed including quantitative questionnaires and
   analysis for the spefific environmental perceptions. The investigation
   using the developed questionnaire conducted in Western Macedonia Greece
   is following. From the study results environmental perceptions of
   landscape values are presented regarding the management of the preserved
   environment of the lake Kastoria under Natura 2000. Citizens are well
   informed in terms of environmental problems in the area. It is believed
   that the study area has a significant touristic value, it improves the
   quality of life, premotes the contact and it is an important factor of
   the function of the town of Kastoria in terms of its sustainability as
   well as it has a leading role to the future of the town It is also an
   important wetland, important fishery and rural place. The community
   accepts in total all the proposed works for the study area with
   environmental design criteria such as aesthetic, protection of the
   environment and besides the proposed works suggested works are
   considered such as cleaning of the lake the security of the visitors
   wastewater treatment plant, road construction and pisciculture works.},
