Organization = {Univ Teknologi MARA, FAPS, Ctr Environm Behav Studies},
Abstract = {Urban heat island (UHI) is one of the urban climatology problems arising
   in the urban development. Trees and vegetation play vital role to
   mitigate UHI effects. This study attempts to assess the effects of
   vegetation growth on land surface temperature (LST) distribution in
   urban areas. Green spaces area within the City of Shah Alam, Selangor
   has been selected as the study area. Land use/land cover and LST maps of
   two different dates are generated from Landsat 5 TM images of the year
   1991 and 2009. Only five major land cover classes are considered in this
   study. A mono-window algorithm is used to generate the LST maps. Landsat
   5 TM images are also used to generate the NDVI maps. Results from this
   study have shown that there are significant land use changes within the
   study area. Although the conversion of natural green areas into
   residential and commercial areas significantly increases the LST,
   matured trees in urban green space will help to mitigate the effects of
   UHI and it is important to sustain urban development as well as to
   provide better quality of life on the urban population. (C) 2013 The
   Authors. Published by Elsevier Ltd.},
