   Antalya, TURKEY, APR 22-25, 2010},
Abstract = {The Gestalt principle of perceptual organization argues that environment
   users perceive the overall configuration of the space rather than
   perceiving its elements separately. Perception of functionality in a
   particular interior space is influenced by the environmental appearance
   in accordance with the person's past experiences. This research attempts
   to associate the ambient lighting condition with the perceived
   functionality of the built environment, hypothesizing that the process
   works through the mood factor. In this initial research tool testing
   state, the research utilizes a set of 3D visual stimuli together with a
   questionnaire self-report to solicit response from subjects and a
   semantic differential method to analyze the data (C) 2010 Elsevier Ltd.
