Note = {International Conference on Architecture and Built Environment (ICABE),
   Kuala Lumpur, MALAYSIA, OCT 05-06, 2016},
Abstract = {This research is an initial approach to formulate appropriate design
   policies and development management responses in planning for the
   continued development of the retail and recreational sectors. This
   research aims to identify the factors that contribute to the success of
   urban plaza and its business premises. It reveals how the lack of
   success of business premises at urban plazas is evidenced when a
   traditional bazaar located next to an urban square was relocated to the
   underground level of a shopping complex. Three main methods of
   collecting data are employed in this research; observation and mapping,
   questionnaire survey and semi structured interview. The research key
   findings highlighted that a high quality of design in retail development
   can make an important contribution to delivering quality in the built
   environment. It is hoped that this research could provide an insight for
   developers, designers and retailers the evidence-based quality
   principles to ensure that new retail developments play their part in
   realizing quality outcomes in relation to urban landscape design.},
